>
> On Jan 12, 2013, at 5:05 AM, Ross Ogilvie <ross@rossogilvie.id.au> wrote:
>
> It's more about the sentence structure and assertion. When you say
> "difficult to imagine", the main assertion is about the difficulty. In the
> sentence {lo si'o ciska lo ro fa'oma'o cu xanri} the main assertion (the
> selbri) is about imagining (xanri). Adding fu'inai after xanri is like
> huffing to indicate that you find the imaging is difficult.
